<p>I was inspired by a bug report on tabulated-list-mode to do more work on vtable.  (Funny how that works.)</p>
<p>As you probably won&#8217;t remember, <a screenshot=true href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2022/04/13/15x10/">vtable</a> is a new library in Emacs 29 that aims at being a replacement for tabulated-list-mode, but with a much easier interface.  For instance, the following is a toy replacement for <tt>C-x C-b</tt>:</p>
<pre>(make-vtable
 :columns '((:name "Name" :width 20) "Size" "File")
 :objects (buffer-list)
 :actions '("k" kill-buffer
            "RET" display-buffer)
 :getter (lambda (object column vtable)
           (pcase (vtable-column vtable column)
             ("Name" (buffer-name object))
             ("Size" (buffer-size object))
             ("File" (or (buffer-file-name object) "")))))</pre>
<p>And results in the following buffer:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14.png" alt="" width="840" height="523" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90163" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14.png 1650w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-300x187.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1024x638.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-768x478.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1536x957.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>The bug report pointed out that tabular displays might be more readable if columns had alternating colours, especially if they are very dense.  This example doesn&#8217;t really have that problem, but it&#8217;s a nice test, anyway.  So I&#8217;ve now made it possible to say:</p>
<pre>:column-colors '("#202020" "#404040")</pre>
<p>And then you get:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1.png" alt="" width="840" height="546" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90164" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1.png 1571w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1-300x195.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1-1024x667.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1-768x500.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-1-1536x1000.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Conversely, the readability problem might be with the rows instead of the columns, so:</p>
<pre>:row-colors '("#202020" "#404040")</pre>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-2.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-2.png" alt="" width="840" height="480" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90165" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-2.png 1801w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-2-300x172.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-2-1024x586.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-2-768x440.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-2-1536x879.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>A kind of a line printer vibe, eh?</p>
<p>And what if you combine both of them like so? </p>
<pre>:row-colors '("#202020" "#404040")
:column-colors '("#202020" "#404040")</pre>
<p>Well, of course:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-3.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-3.png" alt="" width="840" height="480" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90166" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-3.png 1796w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-3-300x172.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-3-1024x586.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-3-768x440.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-3-1536x879.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Hey, that&#8217;s not so bad&#8230;</p>
<pre>
:row-colors '("red" "green")
:column-colors '("blue" "purple")
</pre>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-4.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-4.png" alt="" width="840" height="561" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90167" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-4.png 1521w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-4-300x201.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-4-1024x685.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-4-768x514.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>That, on the other hand, is pretty bad.  Heh heh.  I&#8217;m pretty sure I got the colour blending algo totally wrong.</p>
<p>And while I was poking at this, I also added a divider thing, so you<br />
can say:</p>
<p><tt>:divider-width "2px"</tt></p>
<p>And get:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-5.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-5.png" alt="" width="840" height="583" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90168" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-5.png 1472w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-5-300x208.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-5-1024x712.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-5-768x534.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Or, well, anything:</p>
<p><tt>:divider " <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f349.png" alt="🍉" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> "</tt></p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-6.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-6.png" alt="" width="840" height="530" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90169" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-6.png 1616w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-6-300x190.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-6-1024x647.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-6-768x485.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-14-6-1536x970.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
